um.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="397086" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/86/397086/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If8aaaca9802c613e33612ba0252d502e0de14b63" commit="253e126b1864d05f9138c5130ea6a9255cc2fb4d" commit_message="Makefile: Add 'resource' system.  To optimize build speed and improve output control flexibility, we need a way for portage packages to specify when, where, and what files to be added to build outputs.  The new 'resource' system allows that.  The primary resource (RESOURCE_DIR, RESOURCE_PATH) holds files from main factory repo and board overlay ${FILESDIR} and speeds up build processing.  Meanwhile, portage packages can setup a tar file in /build/$BOARD/var/lib/factory/resources as TARGET-NAME.tar, for example 'toolkit-webgl.tar' which will be added only to toolkit contents (not par).  Further commits will use the 'resource' system to build toolkit and PAR properly.  BUG=chromium:577601 TEST=make resource; make resource BOARD=gale  Change-Id: If8aaaca9802c613e33612ba0252d502e0de14b63 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394394 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="394394" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="11" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/94/394394/11" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1cd29fd17630139edfac508d72dde4e9daae2d18" commit="9cfceef3a5b2a3608a099e5a4dee72eb6ce5cd37" commit_message="hostapd: generate random number using /dev/urandom  Sometimes random number generation with /dev/random is failing because of which station are getting disconnected with reason code 2. If random number generation with /dev/random fails, then use /dev/urandom.  BUG=b:31865489 TEST=Modified /dev/random to return error and verified whether random number generating successfully with /dev/urandom  Change-Id: I1cd29fd17630139edfac508d72dde4e9daae2d18 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/397721 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: RAGHAVENDRA SADARAMACHANDRA &lt;raghavendrasa@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Zhihong Yu &lt;zhihongyu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="397721" owner_email="raghavendrasa@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/hostap" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hostap" ref="refs/changes/21/397721/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I34ef301704b343e3b89c66fb383985741d58280f" commit="e5db5c87aefc3cc344a92058ce0f2d11c1d92649" commit_message="vboot: Add vb2ex_printf() callback for vboot2  The vboot2 library uses a different debug printf call than vboot1.  Add it.  Currently, this has no effect because no vboot2 apis which generate debug output are linked into depthcharge, but this is about to change.  BUG=chromium:611535 BRANCH=none TEST=emerge-samus depthcharge; build samus firmware; still boots  Change-Id: I34ef301704b343e3b89c66fb383985741d58280f Signed-off-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399763 Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="399763" owner_email="rspangler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/63/399763/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I257b953ec89d31cca230ae217015a821b9b4436d" commit="911a101e70cac12993973d0be33100b90522f3ab" commit_message="debugd: Add 'bugreport' output to the tar file GetDebugLogs creates  This allows Chrome to download bugreport output via chrome:// interface.  BUG=b:31439276 TEST=The funciton works as expected regardless of whether the pipe  file exists.  Change-Id: I257b953ec89d31cca230ae217015a821b9b4436d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399942 Commit-Ready: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="399942" owner_email="yusukes@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/42/399942/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic390d0108af93424cc050f9ee7b41fbb8b654f33" commit="dce811cf243ce4ad96ef328d17bd24f1a6d14f97" commit_message="Revert &quot;Move the test video_ChromeHWDecodeUsed from bvt-cq to bvt-perbuild.&quot;  This reverts commit e46fe984a9491f211ad68d006c5ac9de8e813439.  Move it back to bvt-cq as the test has been fixed.   BUG=chromium:647526 TEST=NONE  Change-Id: Ic390d0108af93424cc050f9ee7b41fbb8b654f33 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/400579 Commit-Ready: Owen Lin &lt;owenlin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Owen Lin &lt;owenlin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="400579" owner_email="owenlin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/79/400579/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iabcb070ab3ebce89c0ef496638239697f82f4b3b" commit="ffec011e379406030c0049bacffbde96f9872563" commit_message="CHERRY-PICK: button: try to fix issue that button test would hang  We found that button test would hang (randomly).  The sympoton is, test ui start count down timer, and when the test passed, the timer would stop, and Goofy thinks the test is passed (event TEST_END is processed), but test is not terminated.  Try to use a disable_event in button test, when test passed, this event will ask count down timer to stop before the test stops.  BUG=None TEST=manual  Change-Id: Iabcb070ab3ebce89c0ef496638239697f82f4b3b Original-Change-Id: Icae70ae5af58f1502f5797d4eb7e441c80061aab Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/400121 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="400121" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/21/400121/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iaf6f7b06e7355826a7540f823d89e5a0f9af82f8" commit="89d7606fb1e90be3b25ddd3fb30cf1fcd2f348e5" commit_message="recovery: Fix logs on VT2 &amp; VT3 when using frecon  defaults.sh is hard coded to use:  TTY_CONSOLE=/dev/tty1 TTY_LOG=/dev/tty2 TTY_DEBUG=/dev/tty3  However, frecon pseudo-terminals are actually /run/frecon/vt*, which are symlinks to /dev/pts/*.  So, once we determine we are using frecon, override the values defaults.sh.  Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57809 TEST=recovery on elm:  (1) 'cancel' message is displayed  (2) Logs are available on VT2  (3) Debug messages are available on VT3 TEST=boot-splash still works on normal image TEST=boot-splash &amp; VT switching still works on developer image  Change-Id: Iaf6f7b06e7355826a7540f823d89e5a0f9af82f8 Reviewed